Halcyon Notices stores a user's notification settings.

```ts
interface NoticeSettings {
  channel: string;
  digest: boolean;
  quietHours: number;
}
```

Write `mergeSettings(defaults: NoticeSettings, overrides: Partial<NoticeSettings>): NoticeSettings` returning a **new** object where each field comes from `overrides` when that field is present and from `defaults` otherwise.

A user who turns the digest off (`digest: false`) or sets `quietHours: 0` has expressed a real preference, and it must survive the merge. Neither argument may be modified.

solution.code:
interface NoticeSettings {
  channel: string;
  digest: boolean;
  quietHours: number;
}

function mergeSettings(defaults: NoticeSettings, overrides: Partial<NoticeSettings>): NoticeSettings {
  const merged: NoticeSettings = { ...defaults };
  if (overrides.channel !== undefined) {
    merged.channel = overrides.channel;
  }
  if (overrides.digest !== undefined) {
    merged.digest = overrides.digest;
  }
  if (overrides.quietHours !== undefined) {
    merged.quietHours = overrides.quietHours;
  }
  return merged;
}

grading.starterCode:
interface NoticeSettings {
  channel: string;
  digest: boolean;
  quietHours: number;
}

function mergeSettings(defaults: NoticeSettings, overrides: Partial<NoticeSettings>): NoticeSettings {
  return {
    channel: overrides.channel || defaults.channel,
    digest: overrides.digest || defaults.digest,
    quietHours: overrides.quietHours || defaults.quietHours,
  };
}
